                <pb facs="0459" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>

                <p>[Enclosures.]</p>
                <p>1.Mr. Wilding to Mr. Adams, July 11, 1865.</p>
                <p>2. Mr. Dudley to Mr. Adams, July 14, 1865.</p>
                <p>3. Legal opinions of Dr. Twiss and Mr. Lush—cotton by the Aline—July 12 and 13,
                    1865.</p>
                <p>4. Mr. Druce’s opinion on the same, July 13, 1865.</p>
                <p>5. Bills of entry of Aline’s cotton.</p>
                <p>6. Dr. Twiss and Mr. Lush—the Rappahannock or Beatrice—July 12 and 13, 1865.</p>
                <p>7. Mr. Wilding to Mr. Adams, July 17, 1865.</p>
                <p>8. Dr. Twiss and Mr Lush—Tallahassee—July 14, 1865.</p>
                <p>9. The same on the Sumter, July 14, 1865.</p>
                <p>10. Mr. Wilding to Mr. Adams, July 18. 1865.</p>
                <p>11. Harvey, Jervis &amp; Ryley, on McDowall and Halliday’s course about the
                    cotton, July 18, 1865.</p>














